G3306.b:
⟪μένω⟫,
[in LXX for ⁨עמד⁩, ⁨קוּם⁩ etc.;] ⟪to stay⟫, ⟪abide⟫, ⟪remain⟫.
⟪1.⟫ Intrans.;
	⟪(i)⟫ of place: seq. ἐν, ⟦Luke 8:27|Lk 8:27⟧, al.; παρά, c. dat. pers., ⟦John 1:40|Jo 1:40⟧, al; σύν, ⟦Luke 1:56|Lk 1:56⟧; καθ’ ἑαυτόν, ⟦Acts 28:16|Ac 28:16⟧; c. adv., ἐκεῖ, ⟦Matthew 10:11|Mt 10:11⟧; ὧδε, ⟦Matthew 26:38|Mt 26:38⟧; metaph., ⟦1 John 2:18|I Jo 2:18⟧; of the Holy Spirit, ⟦John 1:32|Jo 1:32⟧, ⟦John 1:33|33⟧ ⟦John 14:17|14:17⟧; of Christ, ⟦John 6:56|Jo 6:56⟧ ⟦John 15:4|15:4⟧, al.; ὁ θεός, ⟦1 John 4:15|I Jo 4:15⟧, conversely, of Christians, ⟦John 6:56|Jo 6:56⟧ ⟦John 15:4|15:4⟧, ⟦1 John 4:15|I Jo 4:15⟧, al.; ὁ λόγος τ. θεοῦ, ⟦1 John 2:14|I Jo 2:14⟧; ἡ ἀλήθεια, ⟦2 John 1:2|II Jo 2⟧, al.
	⟪(ii)⟫ Of time;
		⟪(a)⟫ of persons: ⟦Philippians 1:25|Phl 1:25⟧; seq. εἰς τ. αἰῶνα, ⟦John 12:34|Jo 12:34⟧, ⟦Hebrews 7:24|He 7:24⟧, ⟦1 John 2:17|I Jo 2:17⟧; ὀλίγον, ⟦Revelation 17:10|Re 17:10⟧; ἕως ἔρχομαι, ⟦John 21:22|Jo 21:22⟧, ⟦John 21:23|23⟧;
		⟪(b)⟫ of things, lasting or enduring: cities, ⟦Matthew 11:23|Mt 11:23⟧, ⟦Hebrews 13:14|He 13:14⟧; λόγος θεοῦ, ⟦1 Peter 1:23|I Pe 1:23⟧; ἁμαρτία, ⟦John 9:41|Jo 9:41⟧.
	⟪(iii)⟫ Of condition: c. pred., μόνος, ⟦John 12:24|Jo 12:24⟧; ἄγαμος, ⟦1 Corinthians 7:11|I Co 7:11⟧; πιστός, ⟦2 Timothy 2:13|II Ti 2:13⟧; ἱερεύς, ⟦Hebrews 7:3|He 7:3⟧; c. adv., οὕτως, ⟦1 Corinthians 7:40|I Co 7:40⟧; ὡς κἀγώ, ⟦1 Corinthians 7:8|I Co 7:8⟧; seq. ἐν, ⟦1 Corinthians 7:20|1 Co 7:20⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 7:24|24⟧.
⟪2.⟫ Trans. (Bl., §34, 1; Field, Notes, 132): c. acc. pers., ⟦Acts 20:5|Ac 20:5⟧, ⟦Acts 20:23|23⟧ (cf. ἀνα-, δια-, ἐν-, ἐπι-, κατα-, παρα-, συν-παρα-, περι-, προσ-, ὑπο-μένω).

G3307.b:
⟪μερίζω⟫
(< μέρος), [in LXX chiefly for ⁨חלק⁩;] ⟪to divide⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to divide⟫ into parts: metaph., pass., ⟦1 Corinthians 7:34|I Co 7:34⟧ (WH, R, mg.), ⟦1 Corinthians 7:34|34⟧ (Rec., R, txt.) (on reading and punctuation, v. ICC, in l.); μεμέρισται ὁ Χριστός, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:13|I Co 1:13⟧; as in late authors, of factional division (cf. Polyb., viii, 23, 9), καθ’ ἑαυτοῦ, ⟦Matthew 12:25|Mt 12:25⟧; ἐφ’ εαυτόν, ⟦Matthew 12:26|Mt 12:26⟧, ⟦Mark 3:24|Mk 3:24-26⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to distribute⟫: c. acc. rei et dat. pers., ⟦Mark 6:41|Mk 6:41⟧; as in later usage (cf. Polyb., xi, 28, 9), ⟪to bestow⟫: ⟦Romans 12:3|Ro 12:3⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 7:17|I Co 7:17⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 10:13|II Co 10:13⟧, ⟦Hebrews 7:2|He 7:2⟧; mid., c. acc. rei seq. μετά, ⟦Luke 12:13|Lk 12:13⟧ (cf. δια-, συμ-μερίζω).†

G3342.b:
⟪μεταξύ⟫
(< μετά + ξύν = σύν), [in LXX: ⟦Genesis 31:50|Ge 31:50⟧, ⟦Judges 5:27|Jg 5:27⟧, ⟦1 Kings 15:6|III Ki⟧ ⟦1 Kings 15:6|15:6⟧; ⟦1 Kings 15:32|15:32⟧, Wi 4:10 16:19 18:23*;]
⟪1.⟫ adv. of place and time (in NT time only);
	⟪(a)⟫ ⟪between⟫: ἐν τῷ μ. (s.c. χρόνῳ), ⟦John 4:31|Jo 4:31⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ in late writers (FlJ, Plut., al.), like μετά (adv.), ⟪after⟫, ⟪afterwards⟫: τὸ μ. σάββατον, ⟦Acts 13:42|Ac 13:42⟧ (cf. Cl., Ro., I Co., 44, 2).
⟪2.⟫ Prep. c. gen., ⟪between⟫: of place, ⟦Matthew 23:35|Mt 23:35⟧, ⟦Luke 11:51|Lk 11:51⟧ ⟦Luke 16:26|16:26⟧, ⟦Acts 12:6|Ac 12:6⟧; of persons, as to mutual relation, ⟦Matthew 18:15|Mt 18:15⟧, ⟦Acts 15:9|Ac 15:9⟧, ⟦Romans 2:15|Ro 2:15⟧.†

G3358.b:
⟪μέτρον⟫, -ου, τό,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨מִדָּה⁩, also for ⁨אֵיפָה⁩, etc.;]
⟪1.⟫ that which is used for measuring, ⟪a measure⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ a vessel: fig., ⟦Matthew 23:32|Mt 23:32⟧, ⟦Luke 6:38|Lk 6:38⟧; ἐκ μ., ⟪by measure⟫, ⟦John 3:34|Jo 3:34⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ a rod or rule: ⟦Revelation 21:15|Re 21:15⟧, ⟦Revelation 21:17|17⟧; fig., ⟦Matthew 7:2|Mt 7:2⟧, ⟦Mark 4:24|Mk 4:24⟧.
⟪2.⟫ That which is measured, ⟪measure⟫: c. gen. rei, ⟦Romans 12:3|Ro 12:3⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 10:13|II Co 10:13⟧, ⟦Ephesians 4:7|Eph 4:7⟧, ⟦Ephesians 4:13|13⟧, ⟦Ephesians 4:16|16⟧.†

G3360.b:
⟪μέχρι⟫
(bef. consonants, exc. ⟦Luke 16:16|Lk 16:16⟧, μέχρι Ἰωάνου) and μέχρις (bef. vowels, ⟦Mark 13:30|Mk 13:30⟧, ⟦Galatians 4:19|Ga 4:19⟧, ⟦Hebrews 12:4|He 12:4⟧; v. Bl., § 5, 4),
⟪1.⟫ as prep., c. gen., ⟪as far as⟫, ⟪even to⟫, ⟪until⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ of place: ⟦Romans 15:19|Ro 15:19⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ of time: ⟦Matthew 11:23|Mt 11:23⟧ ⟦Matthew 13:30|13:30⟧ ⟦Matthew 28:15|28:15⟧, ⟦Luke 16:16|Lk 16:16⟧, ⟦Acts 10:30|Ac 10:30⟧ ⟦Acts 20:7|20:7⟧, ⟦Romans 5:14|Ro 5:14⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 6:14|I Ti 6:14⟧, ⟦Hebrews 3:6|He 3:6⟧, ⟦Hebrews 3:14|14⟧ ⟦Hebrews 9:10|9:10⟧;
	⟪(c)⟫ of measure or degree: ⟦Philippians 2:8|Phl 2:8⟧, ⟦Philippians 2:30|30⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 2:9|II Ti 2:9⟧, ⟦Hebrews 12:4|He 12:4⟧ (μ. αἵματος, cf. II Mac 13:14).
⟪2.⟫ As conjunct. (as long as), ⟪until⟫: ⟦Ephesians 4:13|Eph 4:13⟧; μ. οὗ (Thuc., iii, 28, but more freq. μ. ἄν; v. Bl., § 65, 10), ⟦Mark 13:30|Mk 13:30⟧, ⟦Galatians 4:19|Ga 4:19⟧ (μ. is prop, an adv., cf. Lat. usque, seq. prep. or adv.; LS, s.v., and cf. ἄχρι).†

G3361.b:
⟪μή⟫, subjective negative particle, used where the negation depends on a condition or hypothesis, expressed or understood, as distinct from οὐ, which denies absolutely. μή is used where one thinks a thing is not, as distinct from an absolute negation. As a general rule, οὐ negatives the indic., μή the other moods, incl, ptcp. [In LXX for ⁨אֵין⁩, ⁨אַיִן⁩, ⁨אַל⁩.]
⟪I.⟫ As a neg. adv., ⟪not⟫;
	⟪1.⟫ with ref. to thought or opinion: ⟦John 3:18|Jo 3:18⟧, ⟦Titus 1:11|Tit 1:11⟧, ⟦2 Peter 1:9|II Pe 1:9⟧.
	⟪2.⟫ In delib. questions, c. subjc. (M, Pr., 185): ⟦Mark 12:14|Mk 12:14⟧, ⟦Romans 3:8|Ro 3:8⟧.
	⟪3.⟫ In conditional and final sentences, after εἰ, ἐάν, ἄν, ἵνα, ὅπως: ⟦Matthew 10:14|Mt 10:14⟧, ⟦Mark 6:11|Mk 6:11⟧ ⟦Mark 12:19|12:19⟧, ⟦Luke 9:5|Lk 9:5⟧, ⟦John 6:50|Jo 6:50⟧, ⟦Romans 11:25|Ro 11:25⟧, al.
	⟪4.⟫ C. inf. (v. M, Pr., 234 f., 239, 255),
		⟪(a)⟫ after verbs of saying, etc.: ⟦Matthew 2:12|Mt 2:12⟧ ⟦Matthew 5:34|5:34⟧, ⟦Mark 12:18|Mk 12:18⟧, ⟦Acts 15:38|Ac 15:38⟧, ⟦Romans 2:21|Ro 2:21⟧, al.;
		⟪(b)⟫ c. artic. inf.: after a prep., ⟦Matthew 13:5|Mt 13:5⟧, ⟦Mark 4:5|Mk 4:5⟧, ⟦Acts 7:19|Ac 7:19⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 10:6|I Co 10:6⟧, al.; without a prep., ⟦Romans 14:13|Ro 14:13⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 2:1|II Co 2:1⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 1:13|13⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 4:6|1 Th 4:6⟧;
		⟪(c)⟫ in sentences expressing consequence, after ὥστε: ⟦Matthew 8:28|Mt 8:28⟧, ⟦Mark 3:20|Mk 3:20⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:7|I Co 1:7⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 3:7|II Co 3:7⟧, al.
	⟪5.⟫ C. ptcp. (v. M, Pr., 231 f., 239), in hypothetical references to persons of a certain character or description: ⟦Matthew 10:28|Mt 10:28⟧ ⟦Matthew 12:30|12:30⟧, ⟦Luke 6:49|Lk 6:49⟧, ⟦John 3:18|Jo 3:18⟧, ⟦Romans 4:5|Ro 4:5⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 7:38|I Co 7:38⟧, ⟦1 John 3:10|I Jo 3:10⟧, al.; where the person or thing being definite, the denial is a matter of opinion: ⟦John 6:64|Jo 6:64⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:28|I Co 1:28⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 4:7|4:7⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 4:18|18⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 5:21|II Co 5:21⟧, al.; where the ptcp. has a concessive, causal or conditional force, ⟪if⟫, ⟪though⟫, ⟪because not⟫: ⟦Matthew 18:25|Mt 18:25⟧, ⟦Luke 2:45|Lk 2:45⟧, ⟦John 7:49|Jo 7:49⟧, ⟦Acts 9:26|Ac 9:26⟧, ⟦Romans 2:14|Ro 2:14⟧ ⟦Romans 5:13|5:13⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 3:14|II Co 3:14⟧, ⟦Galatians 6:9|Ga 6:9⟧, ⟦Jude 1:5|Ju 5⟧; where the ptcp. has a descriptive force (being such as), ⟪not⟫: ⟦Acts 9:9|Ac 9:9⟧, ⟦Romans 1:28|Ro 1:28⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 10:33|I Co 10:33⟧, ⟦Galatians 4:8|Ga 4:8⟧, ⟦Hebrews 12:27|He 12:27⟧, al.
	⟪6.⟫ μή prohibitive, in indep. sentences,
		⟪(a)⟫ c. subjc. praes., 1 pers. pl.: ⟦Galatians 5:26|Ga 5:26⟧ ⟦Galatians 6:9|6:9⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 5:6|I Th 5:6⟧, ⟦1 John 3:18|I Jo 3:18⟧;
		⟪(b)⟫ c. imperat. praes., usually where one is bidden to desist from what has already begun (cf. M, Pr., 122 ff.): ⟦Matthew 7:1|Mt 7:1⟧, ⟦Mark 5:36|Mk 5:36⟧, ⟦Luke 6:30|Lk 6:30⟧, ⟦John 2:16|Jo 2:16⟧ ⟦John 5:45|5:45⟧, ⟦Acts 10:15|Ac 10:15⟧, ⟦Romans 11:18|Ro 11:18⟧, ⟦James 2:1|Ja 2:1⟧, ⟦Revelation 5:5|Re 5:5⟧, al.;
		⟪(c)⟫ forbidding that which is still future: c. imperat. aor., 3 pers., ⟦Matthew 24:18|Mt 24:18⟧, ⟦Mark 13:15|Mk 13:15⟧, ⟦Luke 17:31|Lk 17:31⟧, al.; c. subjc. aor., 2 pers., ⟦Matthew 3:9|Mt 3:9⟧ ⟦Matthew 10:26|10:26⟧, ⟦Mark 5:7|Mk 5:7⟧, ⟦Luke 6:29|Lk 6:29⟧, ⟦John 3:7|Jo 3:7⟧, ⟦Romans 10:6|Ro 10:6⟧, al.;
		⟪(d)⟫ c. optat., in wishes: ⟦2 Timothy 4:16|II Ti 4:16⟧(LXX); μὴ γένοιτο (v. M, Pr., 194; Bl., § 66, 1), ⟦Luke 20:16|Lk 20:16⟧, ⟦Romans 3:3|Ro 3:3⟧, al.; μή τις, ⟦Mark 13:5|Mk 13:5⟧, al.
⟪II.⟫ As a conj.,
	⟪1.⟫ after verbs of fearing, caution, etc., ⟪that⟫, ⟪lest⟫, ⟪perhaps⟫ (M, Pr., 192 f.): c. subjc. praes., ⟦Hebrews 12:15|He 12:15⟧; c. subjc. aor., ⟦Matthew 24:4|Mt 24:4⟧, ⟦Mark 13:5|Mk 13:5⟧, ⟦Luke 21:8|Lk 21:8⟧, ⟦Acts 13:40|Ac 13:40⟧, ⟦Galatians 5:15|Ga 5:15⟧, al.; ὅρα μή (v. M, Pr., 124, 178), elliptically, ⟦Revelation 19:10|Re 19:10⟧ ⟦Revelation 22:9|22:9⟧; c. indic, fut. (M, Pr., 124, 178), ⟦Colossians 2:8|Col 2:8⟧.
	⟪2.⟫ ⟪in order that not⟫: c. subjc. aor., ⟦Mark 13:36|Mk 13:36⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 8:20|II Co 8:20⟧ ⟦2 Corinthians 12:6|12:6⟧.
⟪III.⟫ Interrogative, in hesitant questions (M, Pr., 170), or where a negative answer is expected: ⟦Matthew 7:9|Mt 7:9⟧, ⟦Matthew 7:10|10⟧, ⟦Mark 2:19|Mk 2:19⟧, ⟦John 3:4|Jo 3:4⟧, ⟦Romans 3:3|Ro 3:3⟧ ⟦Romans 10:18|10:18⟧, ⟦Romans 10:19|19⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:13|I Co 1:13⟧, al.; μή τις, ⟦Luke 22:35|Lk 22:35⟧, al.; seq. οὐ (⟦Romans 10:17|Ro 10:17⟧, al. in Pl.), expecting an affirm, ans.; οὐ μή, ⟦Luke 18:7|Lk 18:7⟧, ⟦John 18:11|Jo 18:11⟧.
⟪IV.⟫ οὐ μή as emphatic negation (cf. M, Pr., 188, 190 ff.; Bl., § 64, 5), ⟪not at all⟫, ⟪by no means⟫: c. indic, fut., ⟦Matthew 16:22|Mt 16:22⟧, ⟦John 6:35|Jo 6:35⟧, ⟦Hebrews 10:17|He 10:17⟧, al.; c. subjc. aor., ⟦Matthew 24:2|Mt 24:2⟧, ⟦Mark 13:2|Mk 13:2⟧, ⟦Luke 6:37|Lk 6:37⟧, ⟦John 13:8|Jo 13:8⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 8:13|I Co 8:13⟧, al.

G3386.b:
⟪μή-τι-γε⟫
(μήτι γε, Rec., L; μή τι γε, Tr.), >strengthened form of μήτι, ⟪let alone⟫: i.e. according to context;
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪much less⟫;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪much more⟫: ⟦1 Corinthians 6:3|I Co 6:3⟧.†

G3389.b:
* ⟪μητρολῴας⟫ (Rec. -αλῴας, in cl., -αλοίας, v. Bl., § 3, 3; 6, 2), -ου, ὁ
(< μήτρρ + ἀλοιάω, to smite);
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪a matricide⟫: ⟦1 Timothy 1:9|I Ti 1:9⟧ (AV, R, txt., but v. infr.);
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪a smiter of his mother⟫: ⟦1 Timothy 1:9|I Ti 1:9⟧ (R, mg., cf. ⟦Exodus 21:15|Ex 21:15⟧, and v. Ellic., CGT, in l.).†

G3392.b:
⟪μιαίνω⟫,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨טָמֵא⁩;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪to dye⟫ or ⟪stain⟫.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪to stain⟫, ⟪defile⟫, ⟪soil⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ in physical sense;
	⟪(b)⟫ in moral sense: ⟦Titus 1:15|Tit 1:15⟧, ⟦Hebrews 12:15|He 12:15⟧, ⟦Jude 1:8|Ju 8⟧;
	⟪(c)⟫ in ritual sense (cf. ⟦Leviticus 22:5|Le 22:5⟧, al.): ⟦John 18:28|Jo 18:28⟧.†
SYN.: μολύνω, to besmear, which also differs from μ. in that it is never used, as μ. in its primary meaning, in an honourable sense (cf. Tr., Syn., § xxxi).

G3398.b:
⟪μικρός⟫, -ά, -όν,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨קָטֹן⁩, ⁨מְעָט⁩;] ⟪small⟫, ⟪little⟫;
⟪1.⟫ of persons;
	⟪(a)⟫ lit., of stature: ⟦Mark 15:40|Mk 15:40⟧ (MM, iii, xvi; on the view that age is meant, v. Deiss., BS, 144), ⟦Luke 19:3|Lk 19:3⟧; οἱ μ., ⟪the little ones⟫, ⟦Matthew 18:6|Mt 18:6⟧, ⟦Matthew 18:10|10⟧, ⟦Matthew 18:14|14⟧, ⟦Mark 9:42|Mk 9:42⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ hence metaph., of rank or influence (cf. Dalman, Words, 113 f.): ⟦Matthew 10:42|Mt 10:42⟧, ⟦Luke 17:2|Lk 17:2⟧, ⟦Acts 8:10|Ac 8:10⟧ ⟦Acts 26:22|26:22⟧, ⟦Hebrews 8:11|He 8:11⟧(LXX), ⟦Revelation 11:18|Re 11:18⟧ ⟦Revelation 13:16|13:16⟧ ⟦Revelation 19:5|19:5⟧, ⟦Revelation 19:18|18⟧ ⟦Revelation 20:12|20:12⟧; compar., -ότερος, ⟦Matthew 11:11|Mt 11:11⟧, ⟦Luke 7:28|Lk 7:28⟧ ⟦Luke 9:48|9:48⟧.
⟪2.⟫ Of things;
	⟪(a)⟫ of size: ⟦Matthew 13:32|Mt 13:32⟧, ⟦Mark 4:31|Mk 4:31⟧, ⟦James 3:5|Ja 3:5⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ of quantity: ⟦Luke 12:32|Lk 12:32⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 5:6|I Co 5:6⟧, ⟦Galatians 5:9|Ga 5:9⟧, ⟦Revelation 3:8|Re 3:8⟧;
	⟪(c)⟫ of time: ⟦John 7:33|Jo 7:33⟧ ⟦John 12:35|12:35⟧, ⟦Revelation 6:11|Re 6:11⟧ ⟦Revelation 20:3|20:3⟧.
⟪3.⟫ Neut., μικρόν, used adverbially;
	⟪(a)⟫ of distance: ⟦Matthew 26:39|Mt 26:39⟧, ⟦Mark 14:35|Mk 14:35⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ of quantity: ⟦2 Corinthians 11:1|II Co 11:1⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 11:16|16⟧;
	⟪(c)⟫ of time : ⟦John 13:33|Jo 13:33⟧ ⟦John 14:19|14:19⟧ ⟦John 16:16|16:16-19⟧, ⟦Hebrews 10:37|He 10:37⟧; μετὰ μ., ⟦Matthew 26:73|Mt 26:73⟧, ⟦Mark 14:70|Mk 14:70⟧.†
